5. THE PACKAGE CATALOGUE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
app/src/main/assets/catalogue.json is original work, licensed Apache-2.0 with the
rest of this repository. Every label, description and consequence sentence in it was
written for it. No third-party package list is bundled here, and no third-party
wording is reproduced — a build-time test (CatalogueCopyTest) fails if a quotation
or an attribution ever reappears in it.

What the research drew on, stated plainly: the target handset's own firmware, the
Android Open Source Project, and two community debloating lists that carry copyleft
licences of their own:
  · Universal Android Debloater Next Generation — GPL-3.0
  · Muntashir Al-Islam's Android Debloat List — AGPL-3.0-or-later
Those lists were read to learn which packages are reported to break what. Which
package breaks which feature is a fact about Android, not an authored work, and none
of their files, text or data ships here. They are credited because their authors'
work saved a great deal of time.

